Act as the Incident Commander during critical and high-impact incidents, coordinating multiple technical and business teams toward effective resolution;
Assess, classify, prioritize, and escalate incidents based on severity, business impact, and urgency;
Lead war rooms , establishing clear ownership, aligning diagnosis and action plans, tracking timelines, and driving decisions until service is restored;
Ensure clear, structured, and continuous communication with technical teams, business stakeholders, leadership, and external partners throughout the incident lifecycle;
Manage technical and executive escalations, ensuring the right stakeholders are involved at the right moment;
Track and ensure compliance with SLAs, response times, and key incident metrics , including MTTD, MTTA, and MTTR;
Validate incident closure and ensure proper documentation, evidence, timelines, decisions, and governance records are captured;
Lead and support post-mortems and Root Cause Analyses (RCAs) , transforming incidents into actionable learnings and ensuring preventive and corrective actions are defined and followed through;
Proactively identify operational risks, recurring patterns, and opportunities to strengthen incident management practices;
Contribute to the evolution of processes, playbooks, runbooks, escalation paths, and operational rituals , helping us build an increasingly scalable and resilient incident management operation;
Partner with Technology, Product, Operations, and other teams to continuously improve incident readiness and response;
Act as a technical and behavioral reference for junior analysts, sharing knowledge and helping raise the maturity of the team.
What you need to shine in this role
Solid experience in Incident Management within critical and high-availability environments, such as payments, technology, 24x7 operations, NOC, SOC, or Command Centers;
Proven ability to coordinate complex incidents and make decisions under pressure, bringing structure and direction even when information is incomplete;
Experience managing technical and executive escalations and engaging stakeholders across different teams and seniority levels;
Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to translate technical scenarios, risks, and impacts into clear messages for both technical and non-technical audiences;
Hands-on experience working with SLAs, operational KPIs, and incident management metrics ;
Practical knowledge of incident management and governance frameworks such as ITIL or similar;
Strong sense of ownership and accountability , taking responsibility for driving incidents from identification through resolution and follow-up;
A calm, analytical, and objective approach to critical situations, combined with the ability to act with agility when decisions are required;
Strong influencing and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to engage multiple teams without necessarily having direct authority over them;
A continuous improvement mindset and the ability to connect operational decisions with their broader business impact;
Clear, assertive, and respectful communication, particularly in high-pressure situations;
Advanced English proficiency , with the ability to confidently communicate with global teams and international stakeholders.

Certifications such as ITIL, COBIT, ISO 20000 , or similar;
